KNOWNBUG
instance_array3.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.o1 == 10: PROVED up to bound 0$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.o0 == 11: PROVED up to bound 0$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The interface ports of the elements are left unconnected, and both
properties are refuted. Each element is given the whole array arr rather
than one of its elements, and the RTL builder then finds no members of
arr to connect the members of the port to. The same split works for an
unpacked array of vectors connected to a vector port.
